# Flockwork

> Project planning for churches. Meal trains, Vacation Bible School, workdays and retreats: Flockwork keeps each project's sign-ups, tasks, schedule and budget in one place, so they are easier to plan and simpler to fill.

- Volunteers sign up from one link on any phone and sign in with their email to take a spot.
- People come in from Planning Center or a CSV. Registration and check-in on the day stay in the tools a church already uses.
- The Planner turns one sentence into suggested sign-ups, tasks, a schedule and a budget. It plans from project details and never sees the people directory.
- Leaders see who is serving, who is away, and who is on too many projects, as plain counts.

